FAQ = [
 ("What is the best bed rack for a 2024+ Ford Ranger?",
  "For a rooftop tent, the Putco Venture TEC rack if you can spend the money: 6061-T6 aluminum, rated 1,000 lb static, 600 lb dynamic and 300 lb off-road, with a no-drill install and a tent mounting kit included. Its Amazon listing spans 2019–2025, so confirm the part for the 2024 bed. For a rack you can move to the next truck, Yakima's OutPost HD (13 in, 500 lb on-road) and OverHaul HD (19–30 in) are the brand-name clamp options."),
 ("Do 2019–2023 Ranger bed racks fit the 2024 Ranger?",
  "Not automatically. The 2024 Ranger is a new truck with a different bed: about 59.6 in long and 48.2 in between the wheel wells, against 61 in and 44.8 in on the 2019–2023 short bed. Some listings, including the Putco Venture TEC and several budget racks, cover both generations under one title. Treat that as a claim to verify, and ask the seller in writing before ordering."),
 ("Can the 2024 Ranger's plastic bed rail caps hold a rack?",
  "Not on their own. On Ranger6G, owners report that the plastic rail caps can break under rack weight, and the common fix is American Adventure Lab spacer kits and nut plates that carry the load to the steel bed structure. Owners also report that trucks built before about mid-September 2024 may need J-braces as well. Clamp racks that squeeze the cap need extra care."),
 ("Do bed racks work with Ford's cargo management rails?",
  "Some do and some don't. Ford's accessory rails are aluminum T-slot style tracks, but a Ranger6G owner notes the slots are wider than standard aftermarket T-slot hardware, and that the rails can interfere with racks that clamp to the bed rails. Yakima says tracked beds need its Track Kit 1 or 2. If your truck has the rails, confirm the exact kit with Yakima or the seller before buying any rack."),
 ("Can I use a tonneau cover and a bed rack together on the new Ranger?",
  "Yes, if you match them. The RetraxPRO XR (T-80338) for the 2024–2025 Ranger has T-slot rails, and one Ranger6G owner runs a mid-height truss rack on Retrax XR mounts over it. Yakima sells a Tonneau Kit 1 for select covers. A Ranger6G thread also covers a 10 in rail system from American Adventure Lab built to work with roll-up covers. Budget clamp racks rarely say anything about covers, so ask."),
 ("What is the difference between static and dynamic load ratings?",
  "Dynamic is what the rack carries while the truck is moving, when bumps and braking multiply the load. Static is what it holds parked, which matters for people sleeping in a rooftop tent. Putco rates the Venture TEC at 1,000 lb static, 600 lb dynamic and 300 lb off-road. Yakima rates the OverHaul HD and OutPost HD at 500 lb on-road and 300 lb off-road. Keep tent and gear under the moving figure."),
 ("Which rack height suits a Ranger rooftop tent?",
  "Mid-height racks near the cab roofline are the usual choice. One Ranger6G owner mounted a rack at 18 in, flush with the roofline, and another's mid-height truss rack keeps the tent under the antenna. Yakima's OutPost HD is fixed at 13 in; the OverHaul HD adjusts from 19 to 30 in. Low racks like the Thule Xsporter Pro Low stay below the cab and suit boats and bikes more than tents."),
 ("Will a bed rack make the Ranger sag?",
  "It can. Owners on Ranger6G report rear sag once a rack, tent and gear are loaded, and some add suspension upgrades. The rack itself adds weight before any cargo: Yakima lists the OverHaul HD towers at 59.52 lb and the OutPost HD towers at 44.09 lb, both before crossbars. Check the payload on your door-jamb sticker and budget for the rack, tent and passengers."),
 ("Does the Thule Xsporter Pro Low fit the 2024 Ranger?",
  "The Amazon listing is for the compact-bed version with universal brackets and says no cutting or drilling is needed, but it doesn't name the Ranger. RealTruck lists the Xsporter Pro Low at $599.95 with a 220 lb capacity. Run the 2024 Ranger through Thule's fit guide, and check how the brackets sit on the plastic rail caps, before you buy."),
 ("Are cheap overland racks safe for a tent on the Ranger?",
  "Only within their stated limits, and many don't state much. The JOYTUTUS listing quotes 900 lb and the OBNAUX listings don't give a static and dynamic split on the pages we read. Both list the Ranger across several generations. For a sleeping load, favor a rack with published static and dynamic figures, and make sure the mounts sit on the steel bed structure, not just the plastic caps."),
]

